libbcrypt 1.1.0 (2026-11-08)
============================

This is the first tagged release. It is the version previously developed in
the "future" branch, which becomes the main version. If you were using the
"master" branch, read "Upgrading from the master branch" first.

New features
------------

* bcrypt_hashpw_sha512, bcrypt_checkpw_sha512, bcrypt_hashpw_sha3_512 and
  bcrypt_checkpw_sha3_512 hash and verify passwords using a salted SHA-512 or
  SHA3-512 pre-hash. They take the whole password into account, avoiding the
  72-byte limit of bcrypt, and are not vulnerable to password shucking. The
  manpage documents how the pre-hash is calculated.

* New hashes use the $2b$ prefix, which is the current standard. Existing
  $2a$ hashes can still be verified.

Deprecated
----------

* bcrypt_sha512 and bcrypt_sha3_512 are deprecated. This only affects users
  of the old "future" branch, as these functions never existed in the
  "master" branch. Their digest is not salted, so hashes created with them are
  vulnerable to password shucking. They remain available to verify existing
  hashes, and the manpage shows how to replace those hashes when users log in.
  Using them produces a compiler warning. If you build with -Werror and still
  need them, define BCRYPT_NO_DEPRECATION_WARNINGS before including bcrypt.h.

Fixes
-----

* The static library no longer exports the internal crypt_blowfish functions,
  like crypt(). Programs linked statically with it got a crypt() that only
  supported bcrypt, instead of the system one.

* The library builds on 32-bit ARM. Tested on x86-64, ARM64 and 32-bit ARM.

* Passwords and password-derived data are cleared from memory after use.

* The salt parameter of bcrypt_hashpw and the hash parameter of
  bcrypt_checkpw are now declared as pointers, avoiding compiler warnings when
  passing stored hashes. The ABI does not change.

* Build fixes: header dependencies, LDFLAGS support, correct paths in the
  pkg-config file, and better support for the BSDs and cross-compiling.

* Documentation fixes: safer examples, the behavior of work factors above 31,
  and typos.

Upgrading from the master branch
--------------------------------

* The library is built as libbcrypt.so and libbcrypt.a instead of bcrypt.a,
  and installed with "make install" together with a manpage and a pkg-config
  file. The header is installed as bcrypt/bcrypt.h under the include
  directory, so use "pkg-config --cflags --libs libbcrypt", or the
  corresponding -I and -l flags. "make uninstall" removes the installed files.

* Random bytes are obtained with getentropy() instead of reading /dev/urandom,
  and sensitive data is cleared with explicit_bzero(). This requires glibc
  2.25 or later. See the README for other systems.

* bcrypt_gensalt, bcrypt_hashpw and bcrypt_checkpw keep their names and
  behavior, and existing code compiles without changes. The only difference is
  that bcrypt_gensalt now returns 1 or 2 on errors instead of values from 1 to
  5. Only a nonzero value was ever documented.

* The default work factor is available as BCRYPT_DEFAULT_WORK_FACTOR.

Notes for long-time users
-------------------------

* Some hashes created with versions from 2011 to 2013 may no longer verify,
  or may have weak salts. See the CAVEATS section of the manpage for the
  affected cases and how to migrate them.
